        {
          "id": 2219050382,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I could imagine 1000 being triggered by valid dissections, with the following:\n\nCapture with Generic Segmentation Offload of QUIC. Many QUIC packets in the same frame.\n\nQUIC packet short header includes some bytes that are from the original frame tvb, but most of the dissection of QUIC is done in a new data source tvb (and maybe another if there's HTTP/3). For later QUIC packets, there might be a lot of items added to the tree at offsets less than the max one added in the main tvb.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
